  "reason": "The current best is config_024 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted, acc=0.7250, 3.60 GPU hrs). All completed experiments use weighted fusion; concat fusion is completely untested. config_002 is identical to config_024 except for fusion=concat, making it the most direct exploitation of the strongest configuration to test whether concatenating modality features (letting the classifier learn cross-modal interactions) outperforms weighted averaging. This reduces uncertainty on the last untested dimension of the best-known architecture. If concat improves accuracy, we gain a new best; if not, we confirm weighted fusion is optimal and can pivot to exploring scgpt RNA encoder in remaining experiments. Expected cost is ~3.5–4.0 GPU hours, essentially the same as config_024 since only the fusion head changes, keeping total budget well within limits."
}

